  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Kamazou Women Farmers Groundnut Oil Mill Capacity Building Project</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Sector: Groundnuts. Beneficiaries: 247 women. Description: KWFCS has been processing groundnuts into oil for years using traditional methods. This project aims to address the Cooperatives constraints by developing its business management, financial management, and technical capacities. The Cooperative will establish a groundnut processing facility, which will use standard groundnut processing machinery capable of producing refined groundnut oil. The Cooperative will hire a business manager, accountant, production and processing supervisor and two marketing staff members. The Cooperative will also undergo a series of trainings aimed at developing the Cooperatives business management, financial management and technical skills. Finally, the Cooperative will engage a consultant to develop a comprehensive five-year business plan that will guide the Cooperative in the near term.</narrative>
  </description>
